                    {
                        "sense_id": "b3fa57e0-36b6-3a38-b473-bf4e9bc439bc",
                        "entry_id": "6a7db46c-69a0-3ff4-92cf-213af27b0af9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A soldier on horseback, especially one during the British Raj."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "India",
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75f69918-fd31-478d-94fc-cca4082c7bc6",
                                "sense_id": "b3fa57e0-36b6-3a38-b473-bf4e9bc439bc",
                                "text": "I have been laboring under the impression that, for soul-harrowing vocal effort, the wild-eyed sowars of Khorassan, as exemplified in my escort from Beerjand, were entitled to the worst execrations of a discriminating Ferenghi, but the Afghans can go them one better."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a008bcaf-02be-4452-80dc-d79858b0ddde",
                                "sense_id": "b3fa57e0-36b6-3a38-b473-bf4e9bc439bc",
                                "text": "Among the latter was Hope Grant, who had his horse shot under him in a charge, and was saved by the devotion of two men of his own regiment (the 9th Lancers) and a Mahomedan sowar of the 4th Irregular Cavalry."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aef0073c-1e61-40e5-b19f-b8f3dba03c8a",
                                "sense_id": "b3fa57e0-36b6-3a38-b473-bf4e9bc439bc",
                                "text": "Hills was struck down badly wounded, and was on the point of being despatched by a sowar, when Major Tombs, hearing the noise, rushed out of his tent, and seeing the plight his subaltern was in, fired his revolver at thirty yards and killed the sowar."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
